## Context

Child of 0754, the author's requested test-guarantee comparison with #6012.
The pinned sdtTest.js source is linked in 0754. It tests cached-pack reuse,
missing/stale pack regeneration, concurrent generation/progress, processor
identity, failures, unsupported inputs and real-worker extraction.

Existing local owners: plugins/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js and scheduler.js;
tests/sdt_sitter_bootstrap.mjs, tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs,
tests/test_sdt_read.py and verification/SDT-SITTER-LAUNCH.md.
0740 owns the ratified session-scoped failure behavior; 0752 owns event-driven
reconciliation. Reuse their tests and logs instead of reopening completed work.

## Work and exit criteria

- [ ] Map the pinned native assertions to the sitter's actual ensure/inspect
      boundary and mark existing coverage before adding tests.
- [ ] Verify current packs are reused without extraction and missing/stale
      source or processor identities become correctly classified work.
      Verify native ensure success means a current persisted pack before the
      sitter reports completion; false, rejection and no-current-pack results
      remain failures with honest coverage.
- [ ] Exercise concurrent native callers, shared progress and sitter lifecycle
      transitions: no duplicate native generation, no duplicated sitter
      admission and no false completion when one caller stops observing.
- [ ] Cover transient failure and recovery across activation, changed source and
      processor identity, and password-protected/unsupported input. Respect
      the different owners of native negative caching and sitter session
      suppression; do not impose native per-call retry on the sitter.
- [ ] Exercise incompatible schema/processor cases without weakening the
      sitter's conservative unsupported-pack policy. Report policy differences
      rather than treating native regeneration as permission to overwrite.
- [ ] Assert that the sitter's own `ensure()` call sites block on a
      stale-processor pack rather than returning early the way `getPack()`
      does, per 6012's "should regenerate a stale-processor pack before
      resolving ensure()". A synthetic processor-version bump in the census's
      path, not only a missing/stale-source pack, must drive this test --
      existing coverage of classification correctness does not exercise it.
      Cite the observed cadence as the frequency this recurs at: reading
      `document-worker/metadata.json` off the installed build showed
      SDT_SCHEMA_VERSION 1.1.0 -> 1.2.0 and the PDF processor 3 -> 14 between
      the 10.0 build (2026-08-17) and 10.0.2 (2026-09-11), three point
      releases, with no changelog line from either upstream repo. This closes
      RELEASE-NOTES.md's correction that eager preparation is a one-time cost
      only between processor bumps, not a one-time cost overall (0754 log,
      2026-09-11).
- [ ] Run the production plugin against the real native service in a disposable
      marked profile with synthetic attachments. Record host version, source
      digests, fixtures and outcomes in bench/results/ and a report under
      verification/ cited here. Fake-host tests alone cannot close native rows.
- [ ] Add meaningful negative controls for new assertions; log existing
      equivalent tests instead of duplicating them. State unexercised host
      behavior and remaining blockers explicitly.
- [ ] Update 0754's matrix and make check passes.

Temporary state belongs under the probe job's tmp/ or managed arena with the
existing retention lifecycle. No author-library mutation is required.
